WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
Choose a supported seated or resting position.

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:11.770
This practice is for a manageable feeling, not an emergency or an experience that overwhelms your ability to stay oriented.

3
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:20.350
If intensity rises, open your eyes, move, contact support, or end the practice.

4
00:00:28.824 --> 00:00:30.094
Begin with the room.

5
00:00:31.794 --> 00:00:38.964
Name silently three neutral things you can see, then notice one sound and one place where the body meets support.

6
00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:00.790
Feel both feet, the back of the body, or another reliable contact point.

7
00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:03.730
Let this be your anchor.

8
00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.520
You can stay here without approaching any emotion.

9
00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:29.615
If it feels workable, acknowledge a feeling that is present at a mild or moderate level.

10
00:01:31.315 --> 00:01:32.845
You do not need its complete story.

11
00:01:34.545 --> 00:01:39.855
A broad word such as sadness, irritation, worry, tenderness, or uncertainty is enough.

12
00:02:01.041 --> 00:02:03.731
Notice what happens when you name it.

13
00:02:05.431 --> 00:02:08.841
The word may fit, partly fit, or feel wrong.

14
00:02:10.541 --> 00:02:14.151
You can replace it with a simpler phrase: something difficult is here.

15
00:02:35.338 --> 00:02:37.428
Return to the anchor for one full breath.

16
00:02:39.128 --> 00:02:41.828
Feel support more strongly than you follow the feeling.

17
00:02:43.528 --> 00:02:44.728
There is room for both.

18
00:03:05.914 --> 00:03:09.324
Now approach one small physical expression of the emotion.

19
00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:17.584
Perhaps pressure in the chest, energy in the hands, warmth in the face, heaviness, hollowness, or restlessness.

20
00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:40.770
Choose an area no larger than a hand.

21
00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:49.030
Notice its edges, intensity, temperature, and movement for only a few seconds.

22
00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.880
Then return to a neutral contact point.

23
00:04:17.598 --> 00:04:22.288
Move back and forth at your own pace: a small piece of feeling, then support.

24
00:04:23.988 --> 00:04:25.578
Feeling, then the room.

25
00:04:27.278 --> 00:04:30.328
You decide how close and for how long.

26
00:05:02.107 --> 00:05:09.317
If thoughts tell a story about why the feeling exists, acknowledge thinking and return to present sensation.

27
00:05:11.017 --> 00:05:14.397
The story may matter later; it does not have to be solved now.

28
00:05:39.114 --> 00:05:42.044
Notice whether the feeling is constant or changing.

29
00:05:43.744 --> 00:05:48.214
It may pulse, spread, contract, sharpen, fade, or remain steady.

30
00:05:49.914 --> 00:05:52.204
Report what is happening without demanding movement.

31
00:06:16.922 --> 00:06:22.692
Try a quiet sentence: this feeling is here, and I am also here with support beneath me.

32
00:06:24.392 --> 00:06:26.282
Keep only the part that feels true.

33
00:06:50.999 --> 00:06:52.669
Include the hands and feet again.

34
00:06:54.369 --> 00:06:55.549
Feel the body's boundaries.

35
00:06:57.249 --> 00:07:01.269
Emotion can be present without becoming the whole body or the whole moment.

36
00:07:29.518 --> 00:07:33.528
Perhaps there is an impulse to act, speak, hide, fix, or escape.

37
00:07:35.228 --> 00:07:37.438
Notice the impulse as energy.

38
00:07:39.138 --> 00:07:43.068
You do not need to obey or suppress it during this breath.

39
00:08:07.785 --> 00:08:10.945
Ask gently: what would make the next minute more workable?

40
00:08:12.645 --> 00:08:19.425
More distance, movement, water, contact with someone, quiet, or no immediate action may be the honest answer.

41
00:08:44.142 --> 00:08:45.092
Return to the room.

42
00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:51.272
Find a color, a straight line, a curved shape, and the farthest sound you can hear.

43
00:08:52.972 --> 00:08:55.592
Let orientation widen the field around emotion.

44
00:09:23.841 --> 00:09:28.401
If the feeling still seems manageable, visit one small area once more.

45
00:09:30.101 --> 00:09:34.251
Notice it for the length of one inhale and one exhale, then come back to support.

46
00:09:58.968 --> 00:10:03.558
Recognize the choice you have practiced: approach, pause, step back, or stop.

47
00:10:05.258 --> 00:10:08.888
Making room does not mean surrendering control or forcing exposure.

48
00:10:33.605 --> 00:10:35.065
Let the emotional label go.

49
00:10:36.765 --> 00:10:38.555
Feel the whole body sitting or resting.

50
00:10:40.255 --> 00:10:45.435
There may be change, no change, relief, tiredness, or mixed experience.

51
00:10:47.135 --> 00:10:49.315
Nothing needs to be declared complete.

52
00:11:21.095 --> 00:11:25.425
Begin to move fingers, toes, shoulders, or the head.

53
00:11:27.125 --> 00:11:30.815
Keep the gaze open and orient toward what comes next in the real room.

54
00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:53.920
Choose one practical act of care after the practice, even if it is simply standing slowly or taking a drink.

55
00:11:55.620 --> 00:12:00.000
You made room in small, chosen amounts while keeping contact with support.
